  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "For which of the following graphs would the trapezoidal rule give an overestimate of the area under the curve between $x=0$ and $x=3?$",
  "worked_solution": "The trapezoidal rule overestimates the area under the curve if the function is concave up over the given interval.    \n\nFrom the given graphs, the only curve that is concave up on $[0,3]$ is the one shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274355/assets/bf44f59745d8fefd48ed9106bbfcbc7e59eba1df0cf0e49fdcb6ca3e9c5a1db6.png)",
